  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear first this morning Case 17-155, Hughes versus the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Eric Shumsky",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In a (C) agreement, the government is giving up, often, certain things. Sometimes they dismiss additional charges. Sometimes, as here, they give up filing a persistent felony certificate. Sometimes they agree not to prosecute someone important to the defendant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So are you conceding there's no -- you can't imagine a scenario where someone wouldn't be eligible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor Re",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Professor -- Professor Re wrote an interesting amicus brief in this case arguing that the logical subset approach is illogical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, in those circumstances, there is no result?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm sorry. Why is the development of the law stunted completely?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, can I just ask you this quick question? Suppose that there's a majority of the Court that -- that agrees that a particular party is entitled to relief, but there is no majority as to the provision of the Constitution that provides the relief. What happens in that situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. KOVNER",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The circuit split here concerns the interpretation of the Marks rule. And this Court should decide this case by rejecting the view of the two circuits that treat divided decisions of this Court as entitled to no precedential effect unless the separate opinions of this Court share the same reasoning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What guidance?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Suppose we say you're absolutely right, and that's why the word \"based upon\" cannot just refer to these hypotheticals we know nothing about. Therefore, \"based upon\" refers to an instance where the judge made significant use of the guideline, either in his reasoning or in the reasons that he gave, which, of course, would throw this case right into the opposite side"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. KOVNER",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KOVNER: So I think there are a few reasons. First of all, we don't think, respectfully, that in the ordinary case, it's going to be easy to sort out whether the -- the -- whether the court was just calculating the guidelines, which Petitioner suggests would not be enough, or was relying -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: No, I understand you'd like us to decide what we're calling the Marks question, rather than just resolving what Freeman means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-155",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1cf2255faab63e8e7b4e77c449a7c9f8113793cf0bdf035226e3b02dd1923e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1cf2255faab-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I -- I'm not in disagreement with that. But the one thing you're -- the Solicitor General's Office said, when a judge rejects a (C) agreement, the parties are put back to their starting point, which means the government keeps its right to file the persistent felony certificate or to prosecute the dismissed charges or the charges it proposed to dismiss."
    },
